The pair’s magnetic moment is represented by the vector sum $\boldsymbol{\Sigma}
  =
  \boldsymbol{\sigma}+\boldsymbol{\tau}.$ Its third component annihilates both basis vectors: $\begin{aligned}
  (\sigma_3+\tau_3)\ket{ud}
  &=(1-1)\ket{ud}=0,\nonumber\\
  (\sigma_3+\tau_3)\ket{du}
  &=(-1+1)\ket{du}=0.\end{aligned}$ Consequently, $(\sigma_3+\tau_3)\ket{\psi_\pm}=0.$ Both sign choices have total third component zero on every trial.

