p.src:
The first component separates them. From Equation , $\begin{aligned}
  (\sigma_1+\tau_1)\ket{ud}
  &=\ket{dd}+\ket{uu},\nonumber\\
  (\sigma_1+\tau_1)\ket{du}
  &=\ket{uu}+\ket{dd}.\end{aligned}$ Thus $\begin{aligned}
  (\sigma_1+\tau_1)\ket{\psi_+}
  &=
  \sqrt2\bigl(\ket{uu}+\ket{dd}\bigr),\nonumber\\
  (\sigma_1+\tau_1)\ket{\psi_-}
  &=0.
  \end{aligned}$ The plus state may have zero expectation value for this observable, but it is not its zero-eigenvalue eigenstate.

