p.src:
Now input a spin pointing right, $\ket{r}
  =
  \frac{\ket{u}+\ket{d}}{\sqrt2}.$ Equations  and  force the output $\ket{r}
  \longrightarrow
  \frac{\ket{uu}+\ket{dd}}{\sqrt2}.$ Exact cloning instead requires two independent copies: $\begin{aligned}
  \ket{rr}
  &=
  \ket{r}\otimes\ket{r}\nonumber\\
  &=
  \frac12
  \left(
    \ket{uu}+\ket{ud}+\ket{du}+\ket{dd}
  \right).
  \end{aligned}$ The mixed terms in Equation  are absent from Equation . The two outputs are different.

